The matched \code{station_id} replaces any \code{station_id} the detections carried.
Detections that match no deployment keep their own \code{station_id}, or \code{NA},
and stay in the set: no row is removed here. A detection or deployment with
no \code{receiver_serial} matches nothing.

Receivers are matched on \code{receiver_serial} as written. A detection that
matches no deployment that way is matched again on the bare serial, so
\code{"VR2Tx-480013"} finds the deployment of \code{"480013"} and the reverse; its
\code{receiver_serial} then takes the deployment's form, which the listening
days use too. Only a known receiver family (VR, HR, TBR and others)
followed by three or more digits is read as model and serial. The log
counts these matches, and \code{detset()} warns when fewer than half of the
